<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

	<!--
		Insect mamono mourn their own like drones, not like daughters (user ruling
		2026-09-27: "a greatly lowered mood debuff for killed colonists, to match
		the disposable nature of insect momos").

		Why a marker and not vanilla's own `ThoughtDef.nullifyingGenes`, which is
		what this patch wrote until 2026-09-29. That field is read in exactly two
		places, and the second one is the problem: `ThoughtUtility.NullifyingGene`
		is the nullification we want, but `GeneDef.GetDescriptionFull` also walks
		every thought naming the gene and prints it on the GENE's own tooltip - a
		"Mood:" block reading "Removes: My daughter died: -23", once per relation,
		twenty-two lines of dead relatives on the insectoid gene (user's call
		2026-09-29: "hide all the lines about relationship dying"). A mod extension
		prints nowhere, so the marker below is invisible, and
		`PMM_Insects.InsectGriefNullifyingPatch` answers the same question
		`NullifyingGene` asks.

		What is marked is the heavy half of grief, and it cannot scale: there is no
		XML dial between the full hit and no hit. So it is a dead child, spouse,
		fiance, lover, sibling or grandchild, and a close friend at -10 or worse.
		Left alone on purpose: her parents and extended kin (-4 to -8), bonded
		animals (-8), and the colony's own generic losses - KnowColonistDied at -3
		and ColonistLost at -6 - which are the token that keeps a dead colonist
		costing her something.

		Both files are covered because vanilla splits the two ways a colonist can be
		gone (Died = died on the map, Lost = gone from it) and they mirror each
		other def for def.

		PMM_Gene_Insect is the shared insect gene, so this is one patch for every
		insect caste, and it covers a woman transformed into one at runtime too.
		Nothing about the mood maths changes with the marker: the memory is still
		gained, still worth nothing, and still reads "(Disabled by gene: insectoid)"
		on its own tooltip.
	-->
	<Operation Class="PatchOperationAddModExtension">
		<xpath>Defs/ThoughtDef[defName="PawnWithGoodOpinionDied" or defName="MySonDied" or defName="MyDaughterDied" or defName="MyHusbandDied" or defName="MyWifeDied" or defName="MyFianceDied" or defName="MyFianceeDied" or defName="MyLoverDied" or defName="MyBrotherDied" or defName="MySisterDied" or defName="MyGrandchildDied"]</xpath>
		<value>
			<li Class="PMM_Insects.InsectGriefThought" />
		</value>
	</Operation>
	<Operation Class="PatchOperationAddModExtension">
		<xpath>Defs/ThoughtDef[defName="PawnWithGoodOpinionLost" or defName="MySonLost" or defName="MyDaughterLost" or defName="MyHusbandLost" or defName="MyWifeLost" or defName="MyFianceLost" or defName="MyFianceeLost" or defName="MyLoverLost" or defName="MyBrotherLost" or defName="MySisterLost" or defName="MyGrandchildLost"]</xpath>
		<value>
			<li Class="PMM_Insects.InsectGriefThought" />
		</value>
	</Operation>

</Patch>
